※ pl4g-test: compile=error diag=4465

※ An array whose type does not say its length carries the length beside the
※ elements, so how many it holds is a thing the program works out while it runs.
※ What the asterism expands into is written into the program being compiled --
※ how many arguments a call hands over -- so it has to be known before the
※ program runs, and only a type that says its length knows it.

fn two(a: u8, b: u8) → u8:
    a + b

fn spread_them(xs: u8⟦⟧) → u8:
    two(⁂xs)

@[startup]
fn main() → u6:
    let v: u8⟦2⟧ = ⟦1u8, 2u8⟧
    spread_them(v)
